The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)
    return -EOPNOTSUPP;
if (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)
    return -EOPNOTSUPP;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because there are no checks for the number of available multicast filter registers before executing the multicast filter tests. If the number of available multicast registers is zero, the driver will incorrectly allow multicast packets to pass through, causing the tests to fail.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)
    return -EOPNOTSUPP;
```
Reason:
This added check ensures that the number of multicast addresses currently in use does not exceed the available multicast filter registers before running the tests. If there are not enough registers, the function will return early, preventing the tests from running and thus avoiding incorrect behavior.

